{"page_content": "Test Organism Duration Eisenia 7-14 d fetida/andrei (Oligochaeta) End points S Reference/Source (i) OECD 207 Earthworm acute toxicity tests (1984). (ii) ISO 11268-1 Soil Quality \u2013 Effects of pollutants on earthworms (Eisenia fetida). Part 1: Determination of acute toxicity using artificial soil substrate (1993). (iii) EEC (1985) 79/831. (iv) ASTM E1676-97 Standard guide for conducting laboratory soil toxicity or bioaccumulation tests with the Lumbricid earthworm Eisenia fetida (1997). Comments Adult survival assessed after 1 \u2013 2 weeks. Important ecological function (enhance decomposition and mineralisation via incorporation of matter into soil). Important food source and potential route of bioaccumulation by higher organisms. Large size/ease of handling. Readily cultured/maintained in the laboratory. Litter-dwelling epigeic species. Standard test organism for terrestrial ecotoxicology. The Lumbricidae account for 12% of the edaphon (soil biota) by biomass and are therefore important prey species.", "metadata": {"doc_id": "b365f145-069a-4e25-a58f-33510dda3480", "content_type": "Table", "filename": "information_requirements_r7c_en.pdf"}}